## §B The stream-path leg-selection mechanism, pinned from shim source (quoted)
shim sha256 42d86d99d42658214e362c2759ecab88a03de005e9ed93e9c1804cbf8c15a386
- `shim.py:25-27` (docstring): "Streaming: for `stream: true` the leg is chosen
  from the response HEADERS before any body byte is streamed; the successful
  leg's bytes are then relayed to the caller as-is."
- `shim.py:61`: `FAIL_STATUSES = frozenset((402, 403, 429))`.
- `shim.py:249-252`: `if status in FAIL_STATUSES: return fail(...)` / `if 500 <=
  status < 600: return fail(...)`.
- `shim.py:254-268`: any other non-200 is TERMINAL (`"terminal": True`) EXCEPT
  `if status == 400 and b"data_inspection_failed" in body:` -> fallthrough
  ("http 400 (content-inspection; next leg)").
- `shim.py:270-278` (stream branch): `if stream:` ... `return {"ok": True,
  "status": status, "headers": resp_headers, "body": None, "resp": resp,
  "conn": conn}` — success decided from the status line + headers, before any
  body byte.
- `shim.py:280-296` (non-stream branch): `data = resp.read()` ... `marker =
  _marker_in(data)` ... `if marker: return {"ok": False, ...}` — the FAIL-marker
  scan exists ONLY here; `_marker_in` (`:184`) is called exactly once, at `:291`.
- `shim.py:16-23`: FAILURE = advance on connection error/timeout, 402/403/429,
  5xx, or "HTTP 200 whose body (first DS_SHIM_MARKER_BYTES, default 2048)
  contains a quota/balance/rate-limit/usage-exhausted marker"; "If every leg
  fails, the LAST leg's response (status + body) is returned to the caller."
- `shim.py:56`: `LEG_TIMEOUT = float(os.environ.get("DS_SHIM_TIMEOUT", "15"))`,
  applied to connect/request/getresponse.

Consequence: on `stream:true` the ONLY fallthrough levers are (i) a non-200 in
{402,403,429,5xx}, (ii) a leg-1 400 carrying `data_inspection_failed`, or
(iii) a leg timeout while waiting for response headers. The r22 FAIL-marker
body bait is structurally inert here.

